# Game chrome layout (tic tac co)

## Centered column (do not break this)

- The app is locked in a **390px** mobile frame (`__root.tsx`) with `overflow-x-clip`.
- Profiles, grid, and controls are a **single centered column** inside that frame.
- **Never** set column width to `100vw − peek` or otherwise resize/off-center the stack for the wheel.
- Board size from `boardSizeForViewport` only — wheel must not feed back into board size. Cap board at **390px**.

## Reaction wheel

- **Visible arc width** = **88% of grid** (`WHEEL_CHORD_FRAC = 0.88`). Diameter is **derived** from chord + peek — never set `diameter = 0.88 * board` (shallow peek makes that look identical to smaller fractions).
- Peek height locked via `WHEEL_PEEK_OF_BOARD`. **Do not** grow peek when widening the arc.
- Circle center sits under the grid; only the bottom arc is visible; rest clipped.
- Stickers evenly spaced around the full ring so rotation always brings pickable icons into the arc.
- Status card + timer sit **below** the peek strip — no overlap (peek container `overflow: hidden`; status above in z-order).
- Drag horizontally to spin; tap to react. No “drag” labels, no star, no Unicode emoji.

## Forbidden

- `playW = viewport − peek` (recenters/resizes the whole UI)
- Growing peek height when widening the wheel
- Docking the wheel to the right edge (old layout)
- Showing the full circle / unclipped remainder
- Letting the wheel overlap the status bar
- Moving rewards above the grid
- Cells below 44px for side chrome

## Rewards

- Left of the grid, absolute (`right: 100%`). Shrink/wrap text if needed.

## Win / lose

- Confetti mounts once for the whole result; minimizing the badge must not remount it.
